    "cases": [
      {
        "id": "source-section",
        "source": "have fn complex_conjugate(z C) C = re(z) - img(z) * i\n\ni^2 = -1\n\nre(3 + 4 * i) = 3\n\nimg(3 + 4 * i) = 4\n\nC_abs(3 + 4 * i) = sqrt(re(3 + 4 * i)^2 + img(3 + 4 * i)^2)\n\nre(3 + 4 * i)^2 + img(3 + 4 * i)^2 = 3^2 + 4^2\n\nC_abs(3 + 4 * i) = sqrt(re(3 + 4 * i)^2 + img(3 + 4 * i)^2) = sqrt(3^2 + 4^2) = sqrt(25) = 5\n\n# Application: conjugation keeps the real coordinate and reverses the\n# imaginary coordinate. The canonical a+b*i form bridges re and img.\n\ncomplex_conjugate(3 + 4 * i) = re(3 + 4 * i) - img(3 + 4 * i) * i = 3 + (-4) * i\n\nre(3 + (-4) * i) = 3\n\nimg(3 + (-4) * i) = -4\n\nre(complex_conjugate(3 + 4 * i)) = re(3 + (-4) * i) = 3\n\nimg(complex_conjugate(3 + 4 * i)) = img(3 + (-4) * i) = -4\n\nforall z C:\n    z = re(z) + img(z) * i\n    complex_conjugate(z) = re(z) - img(z) * i = re(z) + (-img(z)) * i\n    re(complex_conjugate(z)) = re(re(z) + (-img(z)) * i) = re(z)\n    img(complex_conjugate(z)) = img(re(z) + (-img(z)) * i) = -img(z)\n\n",
        "path": "/Users/shenjiachen/.codex/skills/litex-equality-inequality/references/evidence/round-67-cases/source-section.lit",
